<section id="about" class="editorial"><h2>About</h2><div><h3>Biography</h3><p>Katie Kratzer is a contemporary painter based on Mercer Island, Washington, in the Pacific Northwest. She earned a degree in Visual Communication Design from the University of Cincinnati’s College of Design, Architecture, Art, and Planning (DAAP). Her background in design informs her sensitivity to composition, color and the relationships between forms.</p><p>After working in design and coaching rowing, Kratzer returned to her art practice during motherhood. Her paintings bring together intuitive gesture and deliberate structure, moving between abstraction and, at times, subtle representation. Working with acrylic, chalk pastel and raw canvas, she explores material processes including staining, layering and sewing independently painted surfaces together.</p><p>Through distinct yet interconnected bodies of work, Kratzer explores perception, consciousness, energy, memory and the nature of interconnectedness. Her practice is informed by a belief in creativity as an act of receptivity—a means of giving physical form to that which is sensed, received or remembered.</p><h3>Artist Statement</h3><p>My practice is an ongoing exploration of interconnectedness—the relationships between individual forms, between ourselves and the natural world, between consciousness and matter, and between the visible and unseen.</p><p>Working between intuition and intention, I use color, gesture, composition and materiality to investigate these relationships. My background in visual design informs an underlying sensitivity to structure, while the act of painting allows me to move beyond the rational and into a space of discovery.</p><p>Through distinct but interconnected bodies of work, I explore the nature of perception, energy, distant memory, unity and transformation. I am drawn to the possibility that what appears separate may, in fact, be part of a greater whole.</p></div></section>
<section id="studio" class="editorial"><h2>In the Studio</h2><div><p>An ongoing dialogue between spontaneous gesture and deliberate composition.</p><h3>Creative Current</h3><p>I approach creativity as an act of receptivity. Painting becomes a space for listening, receiving and allowing what already exists within to emerge. Rather than always seeking something new, I am interested in the act of returning—to intuition, to connection and to a deeper awareness of what is already present.</p><p>In the studio, I embrace curiosity, allowing myself to move deeper into the creative current without the need for a predetermined outcome.</p><p>Color is central to my practice. Each palette is individually developed, with hues mixed by hand rather than applied directly from the tube. I am drawn to the relationships between colors, their energetic qualities and their capacity to transform our perception of one another.</p><p>Through color, pigment, gesture and the physical qualities of the canvas, I give form to what emerges through this process.</p><a class="link" href="#contact">Studio inquiries ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="available" class="editorial"><h2>Available Works</h2><div><p>For current availability, acquisition pricing or additional artwork images, please contact the studio.</p><a class="link" href="mailto:katherine.kratzer@gmail.com">Request catalogue ↗</a></div></section>
